# Sub-agent / delegated-task announcement

Mirrors `rules/subagents.md` from the EngineOS constitution (this repo's
`CLAUDE.md`) for Cursor sessions. Cursor has no hook system and no EngineOS
specialist-agent registry (`backend-coordinator`, `elias`, etc.) — this rule
is prompt-only, with no technical enforcement possible. Apply it to whatever
Cursor calls a delegated unit of work in this session: a background agent, a
parallel/Composer sub-task, or a spawned tool-use chain — not to ordinary
inline edits.

## Rule

Before starting any delegated/background task, emit its own fenced `diff`
block, on its own line, blank line above and below:

```diff
+ [agent] <short-name-or-purpose> | mode: AUDIT|IMPLEMENT | scope: <files/dirs it owns>
```

When that task's result comes back, before continuing, emit the matching
return line in its own fenced `diff` block:

```diff
+ [agent] <short-name-or-purpose> -> done|FAILED | <one-line result summary>
```

- One block per delegated task. Never batch several onto one line, never bury
  the name in prose.
- Do this for every delegated task in the session, not just the first one.
- If several run concurrently, still give each its own block.
- If a task fails, say `-> FAILED` and why — never let a summary hide it.

## Why this exists

Claude Code enforces this via a `PreToolUse`/`PostToolUse` hook on the
Agent/Task tool (`hooks/announce-agent-dispatch.sh`,
`hooks/announce-agent-return.sh`) as a backstop, because the prose-only rule
alone was being silently skipped. Cursor has no equivalent hook point, so
this file is best-effort: it only works if the model reads and follows it.
